ta-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">(FYI I tend to only review one book per series, unless I completely change my mind on a series, so want to change my scoring down a lot. -- I tend not to read reviews until after I read a book, so I go in with an open mind.)<br /><br />First 90% of the book is around a 3 star rating. -- The rest drops to 1 star, so saying 2 stars overall. -- I can only re-read if I stop reading when they arrive in Montana,the rest just annoys me. <br /><br />I borrowed all the books up to the most recent out so kept going after I gave book 2 a 1* rating on my reviews to add notes. I tend to batch review. I only kept going because I really enjoy a few of her other works under the R.J. Blain name. <br /><br />First book and book 1.5 = 3.5 start.... Books 3, 4 &amp; 5 were back to a 3 or 3.5 star rating and then we get to this one. (I re-read most of this series, ignoring book 2 and skipping the stupidity from about 90% in with this book. -- I'll update this, if I dislike later books)<br /><br />Around 90% of the book, its a 3* then we got to the last bit and IMHO it went off a cliff. <br /><br /><input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="899ce838-ae5d-4f52-a298-6d7493ef7574" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="899ce838-ae5d-4f52-a298-6d7493ef7574">Jack and Melody are about to arrange to have a civil ceremony that'll happen within hours or the next day... they're highly likely already bonded....<br /><br />Jack is then kidnapped, by a new 2nd bad guy. <br /><br />Kidnapper knows about them going to be married, told that they're probably already bonded, but no he still has to infuse Jack with a toxin to make sure they do bond and that they'll then be heirs to rule Maine. Since Melody needs to be bonded to be an heir / rule. He thinks his actions are honourable because he doesn't want the original baddie to become ruler of Maine long enough to sell it to another country. He knows this is original baddies intent. -- Previous book there was a revolt against the king who'd decided to kill his queen for wanting to leave his abusive self... its stated that the lower level powers, due to having numbers can take out the Elites / Royals... and the rebels would include people of those rank to. -- So why would those who live in Maine just happily accept OB handing over their country? It'd spark a rebellion, aided by the other states, same as happened in ND! <br /><br />Jack while back in care of Melody, who has powers that can save him from this toxin, his heart stops. Not near a defibrillator and it was dumb luck one of the nearby people was a lightningweaver. <br /><br />^^^<br />That all makes sense, well except for the second bad guy. But baddies spouting nonsense it normal. Everyone else treating it like it makes sense a bit later is not!<br /><br />Now it comes to the 'huh' stuff.<br /><br />'He almost died.' -- um no, if someone's heart stops and they have to be zapped by electric to restart it, they are dead. They're only alive because there was an electrokentic to hand!<br /><br />They know who baddie is but nothing can be done, because even though he kidnapped and poisoned Jack, it was in a good cause and Jack didn't die! -- See above, if your heart needs restarting you are dead at that point, and the person who poisoned you should be up for attempted murder!<br /><br />Melody wants to punch 2nd baddie who turned up at the wedding for what he did to Jack -- Sensible reaction. Gifting two kittens does not excuse what he did. <br />[q]<br />Jack 'Also remind me to thank Ekram'<br />Melody 'Thank him? I keep wanting to punch him?!'<br />Jack 'Thank him. Because of him, I have you.'<br />Melody's expression goes blank, then from stunned to thoughtful. Instant she realized the truth of my statement her eyes widened. 'We really do have to thank him, don't we?'<br />N/A its re original baddie, aka Melody's uncle. <br />Melody scowled, then tossed back her head and laughed. 'I guess it was a little silly of me to want revenge on the bastard for trying to kill you.'<br />Jack doesn't know which one she's talking about but it doesn't matter. <br />[/q]<br />-- Really? There's only one living bastard who tried to kill you, you idiot. You offed the other one! Revenge was already taken on the person who technically is the reason who met you deluded fool Jack.<br />----<br />And that is when the book lost me and I decided to not bother reading the last.<br /><br />How does this make any sense?! They were about to have a civil ceremony, just before Jack was kidnapped, probably already bonded he already 'had' her! <br /><br />Also the kidnapper, toxin administrating heart stopping jerk got his way because they became the heirs. <br /><br />I'd have liked the book to end with Ekram at the wedding, and them announcing that there was an error, the report that Melody was named heir, to she'd be queen and Jack king, was mistaken. That they'd actually promised to always be there for the monarch/s of Maine, but that they'd removed themselves from the line of succession. Then Ekram being arrested for attempted regicide because there's enough evidence that M/J were already bonded and that his heart stopped. <br /><br />But no apparently the other times of not appeasing kidnappers / terrorists of this series no longer applies!<br /><br />Also its not consistent with how they treat kidnappers / attempted murderers!<br /><br />Kidnapping someone and injecting them with a deadly toxin, so things happen that you want to happen (that would have happened without intervention anyway) makes you a terrorist! <br /><br />Want the soon to be Queen and King of Maine to waive crimes included kidnapping, and attempted murder, get them a breedable pair of kittens, of a breed they don't have hard to get in the Royal States.</label><br /><br /><b>First time read the author's work?:</b> No (Prefer some of her series written as R.J. Blain; GP Robbins &amp; Audrey Greene. - Updated Mar 2025)<br /><br /><b>Will you be reading more?:</b> <s>Not of this series or it's spin off.<s> -- I really like this world even though a couple of the books are total or somewhat misses for me, so a tentative 'yes'.<br /> Some of the authors' works I really like, others I like, some series are 'hit and miss' and others I dislike. -- She's still in the 'more really like or like' category to be rated as a 'favourite' author. <br /><br /><b>Would you recommend?:</b> Maybe for this series. <br /><br /><br />------------<br /><b>How I rate Stars:</b> 5* = I loved (must read all I can find by the author) <br />4* = I really enjoyed (got to read all the series and try other books by the author). <br />3* = I enjoyed (I will continue to read the series) <br />or<br />3* = Good book just not my thing (I realised I don't like the genre or picked up a kids book to review in error.)<br /><br />All of the above scores means I would recommend them!<br />-<br />2* = it was okay (I might give the next book in the series a try, to see if that was better IMHO.)<br />1* = Disliked <br /><br />Note: adding these basic 'reviews' after finding out that some people see the stars differently than I do - hoping this clarifies how I feel about the book. :-)</s></s></span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/95877270?shelf=a-k-a" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">a-k-a</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/95877270?shelf=athr-fave-5" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">athr-fave-5</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/