er because he had heavier stuff to handle? I just don't know. ","rating":3,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1Q66HVB8PHTX4\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw\"}}"},"likeCount":1,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:90085174":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":90085174,"imageUrlSquare":"","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":1,"textReviewsCount":16,"name":"Dawn McCormick","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/90085174-dawn-mccormick","contributor":null,"id":90085174},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AIHOCQU6PWBED":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AIHOCQU6PWBED"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AIHOCQU6PWBED\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AIHOCQU6PWBED","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AIHOCQU6PWBED"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/90085174?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3308896877"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.nQUZUEDYjR-vDw0rYLWooA":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.nQUZUEDYjR-vDw0rYLWooA","creator":{"__ref":"User:90085174"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1612434421660,"createdAt":1588868780976,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1588868923961,"text":"I did not enjoy this one. There was too much detail of the surroundings, and it was very hard to try to keep some of the conversations straight with all of the Royals. The story line was good, but it was jut too detail oriented and confusing at times.","rating":2,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AIHOCQU6PWBED\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw\"}}"},"likeCount":1,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:81996345":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":81996345,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1694320755i/81996345.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":15,"textReviewsCount":847,"name":"Noone","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/81996345-noone","contributor":null,"id":81996345},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1TI8X4CWBA9BL":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1TI8X4CWBA9BL"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1TI8X4CWBA9BL\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1TI8X4CWBA9BL","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1TI8X4CWBA9BL"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"did-not-finish","displayName":"Did Not Finish","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_dnf","sortOrder":3,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/81996345?shelf=did-not-finish"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/5590422363"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.wuHKN5K7TzxMkSRkcRkUTg":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.wuHKN5K7TzxMkSRkcRkUTg","creator":{"__ref":"User:81996345"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1685831713769,"createdAt":1685829423976,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1685831713769,"text":"The books in this series all follow a formula but the proportions of the parts in it kept shifting further and further to the point where this one is almost unrecognizable compared to the first few.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe basic concept was to start with a character that suffers a lot of hardships and was generally dealt a shitty hand but tries to be a decent person despite all that. Then this character gets involved with one of the royal families many of which are a bunch of incredibly cool and quirky people and suddenly find themselves in a high-stakes high-reward situation where they can use their incredible talent to actually make a difference while also getting the prince/princess in the process.\u003cbr /\u003eThese stories felt a bit like they are built on the idea of karma. But not as punishment but as a deserved windfall.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe romance and family part of these stories was always incredibly cheesy and almost unbearably sweet, but this was balanced out by the difficult and sometimes very dark parts.\u003cbr /\u003eBut throughout the series, this dark part of the story kept shrinking to the point where this one ultimately mutated into a cheesy cheese wish fulfillment story about getting everything, riches, new friends, a loving family, finding the love of your life, literally becoming a monarch, etc. with very little of the depth and intricate character work which initially drew me into the series.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eIt's just straight-up lazy honestly.\u003cbr /\u003eI feel bad to some degree for calling this lazy because the author clearly did what she did with all the books and dove fairly deep into the specializations of the characters (rescue diving etc. in this case) and is still able to write convincing professionals at least to a layperson like me.\u003cbr /\u003eSo it's still not even close to the level of most generic romance authors that don't give a shit about anything.\u003cbr /\u003eI want to acknowledge that. But it nonetheless feels like so much less effort was put into these later books, especially this one.\u003cbr /\u003eI want to feel the emotional rollercoaster of the heart-wrenching downward spiral of the MCs life rapidly approaching rock bottom and then a chance presents itself. An opportunity where the MC gets the chance to prove their metal, gain the recognition they deserve, and fight together with the romantic interest through adversity towards a deserved happy ending.\u003cbr /\u003eThat is the formula (with minor variations here and there) that captured me. \u003cbr /\u003eBut this book just skipped the first parts and basically starts with the final stretch towards the happy end which I think is just boring without any of the spice before that.\u003cbr /\u003eIt's basically romance cheese front to back. The characters all collectively act way too blasée about the supposed danger to convince me that the token villain is an actual threat.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eMaybe that is the part that drew the biggest crowd to this series and it really doesn't need more than this bare minimum saccharine love story to keep its fans. But I was looking forward to much more than this.","rating":2,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1TI8X4CWBA9BL\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:30996864":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":30996864,"imageUrlSquare":"","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":7,"textReviewsCount":576,"name":"Mary","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/30996864-mary","contributor":null,"id":30996864},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2C52A3UB4FAN8":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2C52A3UB4FAN8"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2C52A3UB4FAN8\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.F2WocOIuM1VmhoLM\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2C52A3UB4FAN8","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2C52A3UB4FAN8"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.F2WocOIuM1VmhoLM","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.F2WocOIuM1VmhoLM"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/30996864?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3670349766"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.Qy1_PcIZAGi00zxAlpDVKQ":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.Qy1_PcIZAGi00zxAlpDVKQ","creator":{"__ref":"User:30996864"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1606734839988,"createdAt":1606734378207,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1606734839623,"text":"\u003cstrong\u003eone of the best\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eIn this series the characters are always good people, the world is interesting and the plots keep you reading along . . . but the books have a major issue: the MC relationships are almost interchangeable. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eMC women are strong, stubborn and exceptional, MC men are mature, protective and doting, and every one of them has precisely the same relationship with his/her partner. MC men like to be dominated in bed (even Montana, though he’s happy either way), MC women want kids and make great mothers. All of them are bright, super responsible, patriotic and willing make sacrifices to rule well. Their repartee even sounds exactly the same, and that’s a real problem. Maybe it’s only because I read the books in one long spree, but until this book, I was getting really tired of the MCs sounding like different casts for the same sitcom. At least here there was some variety. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI think the major difference in this book was the male MC’s job. He’s a very experienced search and rescue first responder, and the rescue at the beginning of the story was the highlight of the book for me. It also helped that he had a different backstory than the rest of the series’s MCs—while a royal, he had not been raised as one (all other MCs are royal/elite or exceptional lower caste members). The female MC also has a vocation—she’s a dedicated doctor who’s at risk of bonding for life if she saves someone close to death. So the MCs are automatically more interesting people than usual, as are their interactions for much of the book, which is more focussed on survival than repartee. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eUnfortunately, once they get back to civilization and become a pair, we’re right back to same old-same old. The romantic template overwhelms their individuality and they become clones of every other MC couple in the series. Fortunately that doesn’t happen until the end of the book so I really liked a lot of the story. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAnother facet of the same issue: all the books have another MC, the RPS heads of detail, and they have a similar problem with similarity. They’re all long suffering, hyper-responsible and completely supportive (fortunately supportive sometimes looks a little different, depending on the principal they’re guarding). They constantly whip out snappy comebacks and all have the same sense of humor. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI know it’s hard on an author to vary their characters, but I do hope Ms Copperfield works on the problem. Her books are fun reads—they’d be a lot more fun with a broader variety of personalities in them. Human beings have a fascinating breadth to them and build loving relationships in so many different ways that all deserve to be celebrated. Susan Copperfield is a talented writer and I expect she could do justice to a much greater range of personality than she’s attempted so far.","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2C52A3UB4FAN8\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.F2WocOIuM1VmhoLM\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:95877270":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":95877270,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1590947327i/95877270._UY200_CR1,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":46,"textReviewsCount":1818,"name":"Blake","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/95877270-blake","contributor":null,"id":95877270},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A3IO7F5MV1RTGA":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A3IO7F5MV1RTGA"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A3IO7F5MV1RTGA\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A3IO7F5MV1RTGA","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A3IO7F5MV1RTGA"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/95877270?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"lowred-srs-scr","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/95877270?shelf=lowred-srs-scr"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"prefer-thr-othr-bks","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/95877270?shelf=prefer-thr-othr-bks"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"a-k-a","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/95877270?shelf=a-k-a"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"bk-bks-in-srs-i-avoid","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/95877270?shelf=bk-bks-in-srs-i-avoid"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"srs-often-re-rd","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/95877270?shelf=srs-often-re-rd"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"shrd-unvrs","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/95877270?shelf=shrd-unvrs"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"z-r-j-blain-etc","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/95877270?shelf=z-r-j-blain-etc"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"athr-fave-5","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/95877270?shelf=athr-fave-5"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"r-fnt-mod-c-to-d","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/95877270?shelf=r-fnt-mod-c-to-d"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/5637512389"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v2.2023062214.abfa65e4-cedd-4c34-8dc1-b16d2bb14965":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v2.2023062214.abfa65e4-cedd-4c34-8dc1-b16d2bb14965","creator":{"__ref":"User:95877270"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1764324424520,"createdAt":1687445218797,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1764324424520,"text":"(FYI I tend to only review one book per series, unless I completely change my mind on a series, so want to change my scoring down a lot. -- I tend not to read reviews until after I read a book, so I go in with an open mind.)\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eFirst 90% of the book is around a 3 star rating. -- The rest drops to 1 star, so saying 2 stars overall. -- I can only re-read if I stop reading when they arrive in Montana,the rest just annoys me. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI borrowed all the books up to the most recent out so kept going after I gave book 2 a 1* rating on my reviews to add notes. I tend to batch review. I only kept going because I really enjoy a few of her other works under the R.J. Blain name. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eFirst book and book 1.5 = 3.5 start.... Books 3, 4 \u0026amp; 5 were back to a 3 or 3.5 star rating and then we get to this one. (I re-read most of this series, ignoring book 2 and skipping the stupidity from about 90% in with this book. -- I'll update this, if I dislike later books)\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAround 90% of the book, its a 3* then we got to the last bit and IMHO it went off a cliff. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"899ce838-ae5d-4f52-a298-6d7493ef7574\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"899ce838-ae5d-4f52-a298-6d7493ef7574\"\u003eJack and Melody are about to arrange to have a civil ceremony that'll happen within hours or the next day... they're highly likely already bonded....\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eJack is then kidnapped, by a new 2nd bad guy. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eKidnapper knows about them going to be married, told that they're probably already bonded, but no he still has to infuse Jack with a toxin to make sure they do bond and that they'll then be heirs to rule Maine. Since Melody needs to be bonded to be an heir / rule. He thinks his actions are honourable because he doesn't want the original baddie to become ruler of Maine long enough to sell it to another country. He knows this is original baddies intent. -- Previous book there was a revolt against the king who'd decided to kill his queen for wanting to leave his abusive self... its stated that the lower level powers, due to having numbers can take out the Elites / Royals... and the rebels would include people of those rank to. -- So why would those who live in Maine just happily accept OB handing over their country? It'd spark a rebellion, aided by the other states, same as happened in ND! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eJack while back in care of Melody, who has powers that can save him from this toxin, his heart stops. Not near a defibrillator and it was dumb luck one of the nearby people was a lightningweaver. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e^^^\u003cbr /\u003eThat all makes sense, well except for the second bad guy. But baddies spouting nonsense it normal. Everyone else treating it like it makes sense a bit later is not!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eNow it comes to the 'huh' stuff.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e'He almost died.' -- um no, if someone's heart stops and they have to be zapped by electric to restart it, they are dead. They're only alive because there was an electrokentic to hand!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThey know who baddie is but nothing can be done, because even though he kidnapped and poisoned Jack, it was in a good cause and Jack didn't die! -- See above, if your heart needs restarting you are dead at that point, and the person who poisoned you should be up for attempted murder!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eMelody wants to punch 2nd baddie who turned up at the wedding for what he did to Jack -- Sensible reaction. Gifting two kittens does not excuse what he did. \u003cbr /\u003e[q]\u003cbr /\u003eJack 'Also remind me to thank Ekram'\u003cbr /\u003eMelody 'Thank him? I keep wanting to punch him?!'\u003cbr /\u003eJack 'Thank him. Because of him, I have you.'\u003cbr /\u003eMelody's expression goes blank, then from stunned to thoughtful. Instant she realized the truth of my statement her eyes widened. 'We really do have to thank him, don't we?'\u003cbr /\u003eN/A its re original baddie, aka Melody's uncle. \u003cbr /\u003eMelody scowled, then tossed back her head and laughed. 'I guess it was a little silly of me to want revenge on the bastard for trying to kill you.'\u003cbr /\u003eJack doesn't know which one she's talking about but it doesn't matter. \u003cbr /\u003e[/q]\u003cbr /\u003e-- Really? There's only one living bastard who tried to kill you, you idiot. You offed the other one! Revenge was already taken on the person who technically is the reason who met you deluded fool Jack.\u003cbr /\u003e----\u003cbr /\u003eAnd that is when the book lost me and I decided to not bother reading the last.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eHow does this make any sense?! They were about to have a civil ceremony, just before Jack was kidnapped, probably already bonded he already 'had' her! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAlso the kidnapper, toxin administrating heart stopping jerk got his way because they became the heirs. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI'd have liked the book to end with Ekram at the wedding, and them announcing that there was an error, the report that Melody was named heir, to she'd be queen and Jack king, was mistaken. That they'd actually promised to always be there for the monarch/s of Maine, but that they'd removed themselves from the line of succession. Then Ekram being arrested for attempted regicide because there's enough evidence that M/J were already bonded and that his heart stopped. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBut no apparently the other times of not appeasing kidnappers / terrorists of this series no longer applies!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAlso its not consistent with how they treat kidnappers / attempted murderers!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eKidnapping someone and injecting them with a deadly toxin, so things happen that you want to happen (that would have happened without intervention anyway) makes you a terrorist! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWant the soon to be Queen and King of Maine to waive crimes included kidnapping, and attempted murder, get them a breedable pair of kittens, of a breed they don't have hard to get in the Royal States.\u003c/label\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eFirst time read the author's work?:\u003c/b\u003e No (Prefer some of her series written as R.J. Blain; GP Robbins \u0026amp; Audrey Greene. - Updated Mar 2025)\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eWill you be reading more?:\u003c/b\u003e \u003cs\u003eNot of this series or it's spin off.\u003cs\u003e -- I really like this world even though a couple of the books are total or somewhat misses for me, so a tentative 'yes'.\u003cbr /\u003e Some of the authors' works I really like, others I like, some series are 'hit and miss' and others I dislike. -- She's still in the 'more really like or like' category to be rated as a 'favourite' author. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eWould you recommend?:\u003c/b\u003e Maybe for this series. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e------------\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eHow I rate Stars:\u003c/b\u003e 5* = I loved (must read all I can find by the author) \u003cbr /\u003e4* = I really enjoyed (got to read all the series and try other books by the author). \u003cbr /\u003e3* = I enjoyed (I will continue to read the series) \u003cbr /\u003eor\u003cbr /\u003e3* = Good book just not my thing (I realised I don't like the genre or picked up a kids book to review in error.)\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAll of the above scores means I would recommend them!\u003cbr /\u003e-\u003cbr /\u003e2* = it was okay (I might give the next book in the series a try, to see if that was better IMHO.)\u003cbr /\u003e1* = Disliked \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eNote: adding these basic 'reviews' after finding out that some people see the stars differently than I do - hoping this clarifies how I feel about the book. :-)\u003c/s\u003e\u003c/s\u003e","rating":2,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A3IO7F5MV1RTGA\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:12854357":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":12854357,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1776789030i/12854357._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":57,"textReviewsCount":1245,"name":"Diane","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/12854357-diane","contributor":null,"id":12854357},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AJC2WML80OK0I":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AJC2WML80OK0I"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AJC2WML80OK0I\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AJC2WML80OK0I","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AJC2WML80OK0I"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/12854357?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2910247061"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.-7-byDvChwjbAVFr4lmveg":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.-7-byDvChwjbAVFr4lmveg","creator":{"__ref":"User:12854357"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1564103689991,"createdAt":1564102182743,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1564103689731,"text":"\u003cstrong\u003eRoyal shenanigans both benign and malevolent, search-\u0026amp;-rescue skills, lovable cats + romance = quite enjoyab!e.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eA fun (and often funny) story, both for the new characters and for revisiting a number of familiar folks (and hearing outsider-perspective gossip about events and relationships from previous books). Jack's ice powers are (forgive me) very cool, and I appreciate his practical (for a risk-taker with a cause) competence. The way the Maine royal line's talents and bonding can work make for an interesting dynamic. There are a number of dangerous moments to add excitement to the recipe, and one ethically gray character worthy of discussion.\u003cbr /\u003eI did catch a few proofreading goofs (including wench in place of winch, for one UNintended giggle) and I'm pretty sure there was an internal inconsistency or at least lack of clarity re. Melody's first description of her siblings vs. the rest of the book, but it was easy to get past them.\u003cbr /\u003eI'm trying to recall whether there was anything else in particular that I meant to mention, but I think this is it for now. Overall, recommended.","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AJC2WML80OK0I\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:9276938":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":9276938,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1407766154i/9276938._UY200_CR13,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":31,"textReviewsCount":461,"name":"Paranormal Books R Us","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/9276938-paranormal-books-r-us","contributor":null,"id":9276938},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A3L7R959IX5YZT":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A3L7R959IX5YZT"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A3L7R959IX5YZT\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A3L7R959IX5YZT","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A3L7R959IX5YZT"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/9276938?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2900752643"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.oG6ZMNGSu492R3sDRkMpaQ":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.oG6ZMNGSu492R3sDRkMpaQ","creator":{"__ref":"User:9276938"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1564129540342,"createdAt":1564128437032,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1564129540121,"text":"\u003cstrong\u003eBonds Review\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eLove love loved this book! \u003cbr /\u003eLoved meeting new Royals and learning about the different lines of power. Loved the main character and his ability to keep a level head in the middle of pure chaos. Loved getting to learn a little about countries outside the Royal States. Loved the seemingly endless supply of cats and kittens. And especially loved all the cameos and little updates from the Royals we've met in the previous books.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis book was full of the action, love, and craziness I've come to expect from this series and it literally had me laughing out loud more than once. \u003cbr /\u003eI don't think I will ever grow tired of the amazingly detailed world and characters Copperfield has created. \u003cbr /\u003eBonds is an excellent addition to the Royal States series and in my opinion it is highly recommended.","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A3L7R959IX5YZT\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.G2AK09WHHOLPbgpPtd40Lw\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:20345656":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":20345656,"imageUrlSquare":"","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":1,"textReviewsCount":31,"name":"Trish","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/20345656-trish","contributor":null,"id":20345656},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AGZC53OLHSNRA":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AGZC53OLHSNRA"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AGZC53OLHSNRA\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.F2WocOIuM1VmhoLM\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AGZC53OLHSNRA","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AGZC53OLHSNRA"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.F2WocOIuM1VmhoLM","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.F2WocOIuM1VmhoLM"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/20345656?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3338204013"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.PpiFjWyOqhqwwGc7BAPo6g":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.PpiFjWyOqhqwwGc7BAPo6g","creator":{"__ref":"User:20345656"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1589568229467,"createdAt":1589568190125,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1589568229207,"text":"This is a fun speculative fiction series that focuses on a number of societal failings. Magic and the fall of the USA has lead to the formation of a coalition of kingdoms loosely organized into the Royal States of America. The stronger a person's magic, the higher their caste is, and the monarchs have the most powerful magic of all. Those without any magic are considered to be the lowest of lows and are treated abominably. This series focuses on many human rights issues. I was sure I was going to hate it but, instead, I freakin' love it! If you are expecting high literature, give this a miss, but if you need some good, old fashioned escape, Susan Copperfield is a great investment of your time.","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AGZC53OLHSNRA\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.F2WocOIuM1VmhoLM\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:64745377":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":64745377,"imageUrlSquare":"","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshi